A||||1||Fformula88||Tilt Steering Column problem||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||04-04-2000||08:42 PM||||If I put too much vertical pressure on my steering wheel, the tilt mechanism gives away and the wheel goes all the way down.  This has happened while in high speed turns when I need to keep a lot of pressure on the wheel to stay in turns.  I assume the tilt mechanism has gone bad.  Am I correct?  How do I fix this?  Its getting dangerous so I definately want to take care of it.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-05-2000||10:28 AM||||Without seeing exactly what you are doing..... It could be you're pulling down too hard. That would be a driver error. Most tilts will drop if you pull on them real hard, especially if the latch is wearing.  <P>It's also entirely posible the latch in the tilt has a real problem. Likely the latch is worn. The latch is a part that normally wears. The latch gets worn badly if people let the tilt slam. I don't know if you can get parts for it. It's likely cheaper and is definatly easier to replace the column as a whole unit. ||||reg||1
